{
  format: 1
  name: string-search-applies-no-implicit-case-or-space-folding
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#expressions", "§6.5"]
  tags: ["unicode"]
  note: '''
    Attack: hand the search predicates text that differs from the needle only by
    case or by surrounding whitespace, hoping the engine "helpfully" folds or
    trims and reports a match the stored scalars do not support — the way a
    locale-aware SQL collation or a case-insensitive LIKE would.

    §6.5: comparison is over Unicode scalar values with no case folding, no
    whitespace trimming, and no locale. Each expectation is read off the scalar
    sequences:

      subject "Ma" U+00DF "e", needle "MASSE"
        starts_with = false — "M" then "a" vs "A": the second scalars differ,
                      and U+00DF is not "SS"
        the case-insensitive test is COMPOSED, and §6.5 states why it is well
        defined: the Unicode default full case fold maps each scalar
        independently, so it distributes over concatenation. casefold("Ma" U+00DF
        "e") = "masse" and casefold("MASSE") = "masse", hence
        starts_with(casefold(subject), casefold(needle)) = true.

      subject " 512" (SPACE, 5, 1, 2), needle "512"
        starts_with = false — the subject's first scalar is SPACE
        contains    = true  — " 512" = " " ++ "512" ++ ""
        starts_with(trim(subject), needle) = true — the trim is explicit

    The ß value is written with an explicit escape so no tool can rewrite it.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.strfold@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      probes: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        subject: "text"
        needle: "text"
        raw: "= string.starts_with(.subject, .needle)"
        folded: "= string.starts_with(string.casefold(.subject), string.casefold(.needle))"
        held: "= string.contains(.subject, .needle)"
        trimmed: "= string.starts_with(string.trim(.subject), .needle)"
      }
      $public: {
        probes: { $view: ".probes { id, raw, folded, held, trimmed, $sort: [id] }" }
      }
    }
    $data: {
      probes: {
        case: { subject: "Ma\u00dfe", needle: "MASSE" }
        space: { subject: " 512", needle: "512" }
      }
    }
  }

  steps: [
    { watch: "public.probes", id: "w1",
      expect_init: { value: [
        { id: "case", raw: false, folded: true, held: false, trimmed: false }
        { id: "space", raw: false, folded: false, held: true, trimmed: true }
      ] } }
  ]
}
